# Geometry optimization of LiH as its own task: `--optimize --wf=scf`.
#
# This is the composable form of a geometry optimization -- one task that drives
# MolOpt over a reference engine and publishes the optimized geometry into the
# StepContext. It runs at the DERIVED thresholds; scf_lih_optimize_tight is the
# same molecule with them pinned explicitly, and reproduces the numbers the
# retired in-SCF `dft gopt` path used to produce.
#
# The reference engine is whatever `--wf` names -- scf (i.e. moldft) here, nemo in
# nemo_lih_optimize. Everything else in this deck is identical between the two,
# which is the point: both engines are driven by the same optimizer through the
# same code path.
#
# The `optimization` group is what governs the optimizer. Any threshold left unset
# is derived: gtol from the density convergence, max(1e-4, dconv), so 1e-4 here;
# etol and value_precision from protocol().back(). A deck that sets `gtol`
# explicitly wins over that. See `madqc --print_parameters=optimization`.
#
# check.json asserts max_gradient <= gtol rather than matching the reference.
# At dconv 1e-4 the gradient at a given geometry depends on where each SCF started
# (the previous step's orbitals vs. the atomic guess) by up to ~7e-5, so where
# the optimizer stops inside gtol is not a reproducible number.
#
# Starts 0.015 bohr inside the HF minimum, which the optimizer closes in two steps.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --optimize --wf=scf scf_lih_optimize.in)

optimization
    maxiter     10
end

dft
    xc          hf
    protocol    [1e-4, 1e-6]
    dconv       1e-4
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    Li  0.0  0.0  0.0
    H   0.0  0.0  3.05
end
